# Case Study: Operation Dental

Operation Dental is a people-first dental group with 18+ practices (and growing) that uses technology to scale while maintaining exceptional patient experiences.

## The Challenge
- Traditional scheduling tools limited flexibility and scalability  
- Difficulty connecting marketing investments to actual patient acquisition and practice success  
- Lack of control over scheduling experiences across multiple practices  

## The Solution
Operation Dental implemented the **Synchronizer API** to rebuild its online scheduler directly into each practice’s website.

This gave their team flexibility over how patients book appointments, how availability syncs across systems, and how each new practice launches—all within a **HIPAA-compliant environment**.

Working closely with Synchronizer API by NexHealth, Operation Dental’s marketing and technical teams aligned scheduling, operations, and growth strategy under one connected system.

> “That was one of the big drivers for us to rework the scheduler so we could align our investments with real patient growth.”  
> — **Dave Womble**, Chief Marketing Officer, Operation Dental  

## Results
- **10–25% increase** in new patient growth across practices  
- **Hundreds of thousands saved** annually through efficiency gains  
- **100+ patients pre-booked** for each new practice launch  
- **20–25%** of new patients booking online through the scheduler  
- **Confidence** to scale and direct budgets where they have the most impact  
- All operations running securely in a **HIPAA-compliant environment**  

## Why It Mattered
For Operation Dental, the Synchronizer API became more than a technical integration—it became a **growth engine**.  
By combining NexHealth’s core platform with their own custom-built workflows, they built a scalable marketing and scheduling system that drives measurable ROI, innovation, and patient growth.

The next phase of innovation includes embedding **chatbots** powered by NexHealth’s Messaging API to further automate patient communication and scheduling.

